//@ compile-fail
//@ error-pattern: return type
//@ description: SELFHOST_PASS: `return <expr>` requires a declared return type (E008)
// A function with no return annotation lowers its return type to TyUnknown,
// which types_compatible treats as a wildcard. That made every value return in
// an unannotated function typecheck, whatever it returned, while lean_single
// and the raw compile path rejected the same code -- the split that shipped
// examples/hello.sio ill-typed and red in real_language_runner_gate 6/7.
//
// The trailing-expression form stays legal and is covered by
// tests/run-pass/return_unannotated_inference.sio; only the explicit value
// return is an error here.
fn implicit_unit() with IO {
    println("side effect")
    return 0
}

fn main() -> i32 with IO {
    implicit_unit()
    return 0
}
